{"term":"integrate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:810d617c3aacc83bf2","definition":"To include as a constituent part or functionality.","example":"They were keen to integrate their new skills into the performance.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["assimilate"],"antonyms":["disintegrate","divide","extract","segregate","unincorporate"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cointegrate","disintegrate","integrase","integrator","misintegrate","osseointegrate","reintegrate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:66ba0ec0f777385430","definition":"To join a group or an environment harmoniously; to make oneself fit in.","example":"The refugees integrated well into the community.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fuse","merge","incorporate","swallow","absorb","add on","co-opt","corporate","incorpse","integrate","subsume"],"antonyms":["disintegrate","divide","extract","segregate","unincorporate"],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive, sometimes, usually","register":"intransitive, reflexive, sometimes, usually","wordFamily":["cointegrate","disintegrate","integrase","integrator","misintegrate","osseointegrate","reintegrate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f4f62f90920739634f","definition":"To form into one whole; to make entire; to complete; to renew; to restore; to perfect.","example":"Virtually free of pain, she has integrated the broken pieces of her life, is a loving and loved wife and mother, and is back at her job.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["embody"],"antonyms":["disintegrate","divide","extract","segregate","unincorporate"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cointegrate","disintegrate","integrase","integrator","misi